WEBVTT

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:12.110
It's morning!

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:24.160
Yunocchi, come out and play!

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:26.120
Oh, it's Miya-chan.

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:29.130
It's still six!

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:30.710
Yunocchi!

00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:32.590
Coming.

00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:37.470
Wow! Everything's white!

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:40.640
It snowed all night.

00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:42.280
All right, Yunocchi.

00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:44.560
Go ahead and take the commemorative first step!

00:00:45.950 --> 00:00:47.700
No, you do it, Miya-chan!

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:49.840
No, you should.

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:51.400
Miya-chan!

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:54.740
Good morning, Yuno-san, Miyako-san.

00:00:55.990 --> 00:00:58.450
This is a lot of snow!

00:01:17.590 --> 00:01:20.180
youki ni kuchibue fuite

00:01:17.590 --> 00:01:20.180
Whistling a cheerful tune

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:22.510
madobe no kotori to sesshon

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:22.510
I join the birds chirping by the window

00:01:22.510 --> 00:01:25.430
suima ga yatte kite

00:01:22.510 --> 00:01:25.430
When fatigue strikes

00:01:25.430 --> 00:01:28.060
atama ga danshingu

00:01:25.430 --> 00:01:28.060
My imagination runs wild

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:30.520
nan demo kan demo waraeru nichijou

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:30.520
Everything in life makes me smile

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:33.360
okimari na kishoutenketsu

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:33.360
Nothing really new takes place

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:35.990
demo demo tama ni wa piritto supaisu

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:35.990
But sometimes it's exciting to spice things up

00:01:35.990 --> 00:01:38.610
aozora peintingu

00:01:35.990 --> 00:01:38.610
Let's paint it on the blue sky

00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:39.660
doko ikou

00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:39.660
Where should we go?

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:41.240
koko ni iyou

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:41.240
Let's stay here

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:42.240
sore wa nani

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:42.240
What's that?

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:43.830
are yaritai

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:43.830
I wanna try that!

00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:46.410
ima ni tokubetsu na shirushi

00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:46.410
Let's make this moment count

00:01:46.410 --> 00:01:51.790
tokeibari no mawashikata watashi shidai kamo

00:01:46.410 --> 00:01:51.790
How fast my clock moves is all up to me

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:55.460
shiki oriori iro toridori

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:55.460
With a rich palette of colors from the four seasons

00:01:55.460 --> 00:01:57.920
nonbiri na everyday

00:01:55.460 --> 00:01:57.920
Our laid-back everyday lives can be

00:01:57.920 --> 00:02:00.550
pasuteru bibiddo metoro

00:01:57.920 --> 00:02:00.550
Any blend of pastel, vivid, and metro colors

00:02:00.550 --> 00:02:03.390
jibun dake no karaaringu

00:02:00.550 --> 00:02:03.390
Anyone can create their own coloring

00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:05.970
sono tokidoki mune doki doki

00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:05.970
So when your heart races in excitement

00:02:05.970 --> 00:02:09.690
hachamecha na taiyou ni oegaki

00:02:05.970 --> 00:02:09.690
Just draw a sun at the top

00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:13.820
tobidasu aatishizumu

00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:13.820
And let your inner artist take you from there

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:17.150
gyutto shite ii kana

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:17.150
Can I hold your hand tight?

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:24.530
suki suki suki wo sukecchi

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:24.530
I've been sketching everything I love

00:02:24.530 --> 00:02:27.070
nijiiro ni somete iku yo

00:02:24.530 --> 00:02:27.070
And painting them in rainbow colors

00:02:27.070 --> 00:02:31.830
sore ja ittekimasu

00:02:27.070 --> 00:02:31.830
All right, I'm off to have some more fun!

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:37.010
December 2nd, An Educational Snowball Fight

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:39.990
Sorry I took so long.

00:02:39.990 --> 00:02:41.950
The weather got so cold overnight!

00:02:41.950 --> 00:02:44.640
Yeah, a huge wave of cold swept over us!

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:45.520
Huh?

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:48.520
You're not wearing a coat?

00:02:49.720 --> 00:02:53.650
I <i>do</i> have one my big brother sent me.

00:02:53.650 --> 00:02:56.010
Oh, then you should put it on!

00:03:01.370 --> 00:03:03.550
But he's kind of a big guy.

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:05.890
Yunocchi, you wanna try it on too?

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:10.710
I have to wear it like this to keep it off the ground.

00:03:10.710 --> 00:03:12.610
It looks like a headdress!

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:25.010
G-Good morning!

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:29.670
I dressed up as a snow-woman spirit today!

00:03:29.670 --> 00:03:32.670
But it turned out to be a little <i>too</i> cold!

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:37.530
B-But since I had it on already,
I wanted to show it to you all.

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:39.650
So I endured it!

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:42.700
Put some effort toward something that's actually important.

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:47.010
Since there's a lot of snow outside,

00:03:47.010 --> 00:03:49.500
let's take a look at this verse.

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:50.830
"'Tis not blooming snow

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:51.950
drifting in the tempest's breath

00:03:51.950 --> 00:03:53.310
'round the garden court

00:03:53.310 --> 00:03:54.630
that withers and falls away.

00:03:54.630 --> 00:03:55.840
It is only I."

00:03:55.840 --> 00:03:59.170
I like how they use "'tis" in old poems.

00:03:59.170 --> 00:04:01.090
It has a nice ring to it.

00:04:02.660 --> 00:04:04.350
I composed a tanka!

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:06.350
"A sound with no end

00:04:06.350 --> 00:04:07.390
resonates in my stomach,

00:04:07.390 --> 00:04:08.440
a thundering groan.

00:04:08.440 --> 00:04:09.610
This is what I want to eat:

00:04:09.610 --> 00:04:10.850
'tis a large, fried tofu, please.

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:12.980
Miya-chan, that's not what I had in mind.

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:17.150
I'm like a snow-child spirit!

00:04:17.150 --> 00:04:19.330
Right, Kuwahara-sensei?

00:04:19.330 --> 00:04:23.290
Yoshinoya-sensei, please go warm up somewhere else.

00:04:23.290 --> 00:04:27.540
Kuwahara-sensei, I have a class next period, so may I borrow this?

00:04:27.540 --> 00:04:28.540
You may not!

00:04:31.540 --> 00:04:35.790
During the week before exams, club
meetings may not be held after school.

00:04:35.790 --> 00:04:41.130
Students, please don't stay on campus and return to your homes.

00:04:35.790 --> 00:04:39.170
Yunocchi, let's hurry up so we can have a snowball fight!

00:04:39.170 --> 00:04:41.130
Yeah! I'm not gonna lose, though!

00:04:41.130 --> 00:04:43.010
Hey, you girls!

00:04:43.010 --> 00:04:46.300
Did you not hear the announcement just now?

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:49.060
Principal!

00:04:49.060 --> 00:04:50.680
Well, um...

00:04:51.660 --> 00:04:55.910
There's this popular thing called educational snowball fights!

00:04:56.770 --> 00:05:01.030
I had no idea such a study method existed.

00:05:01.030 --> 00:05:05.870
Teach me how educational snowball fights work!

00:05:06.680 --> 00:05:08.030
Please!

00:05:10.220 --> 00:05:12.550
Sorry!

00:05:10.900 --> 00:05:13.190
Yunocchi, wait!

00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:16.710
We're going to start the demonstration now!

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:18.960
Now...

00:05:24.840 --> 00:05:29.310
Well, now we <i>have</i> to do it since we told the principal that we would.

00:05:29.310 --> 00:05:31.730
Huh? You mean an "educational" snowball fight?

00:05:31.730 --> 00:05:32.430
Yeah!

00:05:35.350 --> 00:05:35.940
Take!

00:05:38.690 --> 00:05:39.820
Took!

00:05:39.820 --> 00:05:40.950
Taken!

00:05:40.950 --> 00:05:41.990
Go!

00:05:41.990 --> 00:05:43.030
Went!

00:05:43.030 --> 00:05:43.940
Gone!

00:05:44.950 --> 00:05:45.990
Come!

00:05:45.990 --> 00:05:46.810
Came!

00:05:46.810 --> 00:05:48.830
What are you doing?

00:05:48.830 --> 00:05:50.390
Oh, Norisuke-san.

00:05:50.390 --> 00:05:52.200
Would you like to join us?

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:55.370
Do you mean playing in the snow or studying?

00:05:55.370 --> 00:05:57.580
What were you doing, Nori-chan?

00:05:57.580 --> 00:05:59.840
I was... studying.

00:06:00.590 --> 00:06:02.370
Nori-tan, I'm impressed!

00:06:02.370 --> 00:06:06.340
Yeah, I hadn't even planned on beginning until after sunset.

00:06:07.340 --> 00:06:12.330
<i>I </i>was<i> going to study, but I ended up wasting time on the Internet,</i>

00:06:12.330 --> 00:06:15.450
<i>so I have yet to actually get started.</i>

00:06:16.230 --> 00:06:17.600
<i>I might as well join them.</i>

00:06:19.190 --> 00:06:23.410
It'd be a shame to not join in the fun when there's all this snow around.

00:06:23.410 --> 00:06:24.570
Yeah, Nori-chan.

00:06:24.570 --> 00:06:25.950
Leave <i>no regrets!</i>

00:06:25.950 --> 00:06:27.780
That just inspired me!

00:06:27.780 --> 00:06:30.570
Here's a tanka about Nori-chan!

00:06:30.570 --> 00:06:31.580
Huh?

00:06:31.580 --> 00:06:33.010
"Nori-chan is here

00:06:33.010 --> 00:06:34.230
so she leaves <i>no regrets on</i>

00:06:34.230 --> 00:06:35.580
this snow-ridden day."

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:36.830
And the last two lines?

00:06:37.340 --> 00:06:38.830
Let's see...

00:06:40.840 --> 00:06:43.090
"Hey, nobody's as naughty as Nori!"

00:06:43.090 --> 00:06:45.710
I don't even know where to start with her.

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:51.210
I have to do well on the exams this time.

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:55.350
I didn't do too well last time, so I want to give my parents good news.

00:06:56.230 --> 00:07:00.290
They're paying my tuition and rent so I can attend Yamabuki.

00:07:00.290 --> 00:07:02.730
I gotta focus on studying.

00:07:03.080 --> 00:07:05.820
I really want to play with you,
but I'll have to pass this time.

00:07:08.320 --> 00:07:09.610
A... A hole!

00:07:09.610 --> 00:07:11.450
We need to dig a hole and bury ourselves in it!

00:07:21.630 --> 00:07:24.380
Nori-chan, whatcha doing?

00:07:24.380 --> 00:07:25.710
I'm studying.

00:07:26.060 --> 00:07:28.530
Did you want to hang out with me, Nazuna?

00:07:29.050 --> 00:07:32.470
No, I'm here t-to study.

00:07:33.920 --> 00:07:35.170
"Nazuna-dono,

00:07:35.170 --> 00:07:36.230
seeing the piles of white snow,

00:07:36.230 --> 00:07:37.290
wants to play in it.

00:07:37.290 --> 00:07:38.440
But Norippe must study

00:07:38.440 --> 00:07:40.310
to pass her exams.

00:07:44.320 --> 00:07:46.150
Hey, Hiro.

00:07:46.580 --> 00:07:51.030
We're studying together like it's nothing special now,

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:55.160
but I don't think it's something
you can do with just anyone.

00:07:55.160 --> 00:07:59.160
It has to be someone you can get along with.

00:07:59.160 --> 00:08:01.920
And we met each other here,

00:08:01.920 --> 00:08:04.330
which was really lucky, at least in my opinion.

00:08:05.420 --> 00:08:06.920
Just saying.

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:10.670
Sorry for saying weird stuff out of nowhere.

00:08:11.280 --> 00:08:12.550
Sae?

00:08:15.430 --> 00:08:16.870
"Sae and Hiro.

00:08:16.870 --> 00:08:17.900
While they are supposedly

00:08:17.900 --> 00:08:19.130
on the same wavelength,

00:08:19.130 --> 00:08:20.300
it turns out that Hiro-san

00:08:20.300 --> 00:08:21.940
wasn't even listening."

00:08:21.940 --> 00:08:23.290
Miya-chan?

00:08:31.920 --> 00:08:33.700
Have some hot milk.

00:08:34.700 --> 00:08:36.780
Thank you, Hiro-san!

00:08:40.140 --> 00:08:42.730
It's nice to watch the snow fall at night.

00:08:42.730 --> 00:08:45.030
Makes me want to recite another tanka.

00:08:45.030 --> 00:08:47.170
Oh, classy.

00:08:47.170 --> 00:08:48.920
We went over one in class today.

00:08:48.920 --> 00:08:52.680
"'Tis not blooming snow drifting in the
tempest's breath 'round the garden court..."

00:08:52.680 --> 00:08:54.070
Oh.

00:08:54.070 --> 00:08:56.680
That's not a poem about snow, though.

00:08:58.440 --> 00:09:00.720
I thought you went over it in class.

00:09:01.850 --> 00:09:02.870
How is it?

00:09:02.870 --> 00:09:04.480
Are you making progress with your studies?

00:09:04.480 --> 00:09:06.210
Oh, well, um...

00:09:06.940 --> 00:09:11.810
Nori-chan, is it actually hard for you to study while I'm around?

00:09:11.810 --> 00:09:14.970
All I do is ask you questions.

00:09:14.970 --> 00:09:17.510
No, not at all.

00:09:17.510 --> 00:09:20.490
Answering them helps me review too,

00:09:20.490 --> 00:09:22.580
and it keeps me from getting distracted by the Internet.

00:09:23.020 --> 00:09:24.710
That's a relief.

00:09:24.710 --> 00:09:29.650
Oh yeah, it's pretty easy to get sidetracked when you're studying alone.

00:09:29.650 --> 00:09:33.370
Yeah, if Yunocchi hadn't invited me to her study session,

00:09:33.370 --> 00:09:36.370
I might have composed a Hidamari tanka anthology.

00:09:36.370 --> 00:09:38.470
You've composed that many already?

00:09:38.600 --> 00:09:40.970
'Tis Heaven under the kotatsu!

00:09:40.970 --> 00:09:42.150
Hey, Miyako!

00:09:42.150 --> 00:09:43.850
It's so cozy!

00:09:43.850 --> 00:09:47.940
I wish our desks at school had kotatsus installed too.

00:09:47.940 --> 00:09:49.210
Yeah, that'd be nice.

00:09:49.210 --> 00:09:52.440
And on the side, there should be mandarin oranges!

00:09:53.640 --> 00:09:56.150
During afternoon classes, when everybody is full,

00:09:56.150 --> 00:09:58.070
they could take a nap!

00:09:58.070 --> 00:10:01.080
It's something we've all fantasized about.

00:10:02.010 --> 00:10:04.580
I want to carry the kotatsu on my back to school.

00:10:04.580 --> 00:10:06.460
Miya-chan, you'd be like a turtle!

00:10:16.480 --> 00:10:18.250
Time for a verse!

00:10:18.970 --> 00:10:20.490
"Although 'tis snowing,

00:10:20.490 --> 00:10:21.680
Hidamari's lights

00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:23.070
still shine through the panes.

00:10:23.070 --> 00:10:24.380
Listen closely and you'll hear

00:10:24.380 --> 00:10:25.950
the girls laughing merrily.

00:10:35.270 --> 00:10:36.780
Hey, Hiro.

00:10:36.780 --> 00:10:40.150
Chika might be coming over today.

00:10:40.150 --> 00:10:40.990
Huh?

00:10:40.990 --> 00:10:45.250
Even if she does come, you don't have to put out food or anything like that.

00:10:45.250 --> 00:10:47.110
O-Okay.

00:10:47.110 --> 00:10:50.410
I woke up this morning and saw a text from her about it.

00:10:50.410 --> 00:10:52.040
On such short notice, too.

00:10:54.290 --> 00:10:57.170
Maybe we should have another big gyoza party.

00:10:57.170 --> 00:10:59.340
Hiro, were you listening to me at all?

00:11:01.590 --> 00:11:03.220
I'm here~!

00:11:01.590 --> 00:11:03.220
How come you're not

00:11:01.590 --> 00:11:03.220
in your room?

00:11:04.800 --> 00:11:06.470
Whoa, seriously?

00:11:10.480 --> 00:11:12.060
There you are!

00:11:12.060 --> 00:11:15.310
I almost thought you were pretending not to be home.

00:11:15.310 --> 00:11:17.650
Long time no see, Chika-chan!

00:11:17.650 --> 00:11:20.290
Hiro-san, it's been a while!

00:11:20.290 --> 00:11:22.150
What's going on?

00:11:22.150 --> 00:11:24.660
Want to come in and have some tea?

00:11:24.660 --> 00:11:28.620
Oh no, I'm here as a messenger today!

00:11:28.940 --> 00:11:31.830
As much as I'd like to have tea with you,

00:11:31.830 --> 00:11:33.620
my duties come first!

00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:37.250
I'll be borrowing my sister for a bit.

00:11:41.590 --> 00:11:46.600
December 15th, Hidamari Cheer Team

00:11:49.010 --> 00:11:50.850
You could've been nicer.

00:11:50.850 --> 00:11:53.010
I don't want to hear that from
someone who just barged in.

00:11:53.010 --> 00:11:55.390
Is that how you're gonna treat me?

00:11:55.390 --> 00:11:59.270
I have an important message from Mom and Dad!

00:12:00.760 --> 00:12:04.400
It's about your mock exam results that were mailed to us the other day!

00:12:11.480 --> 00:12:13.270
What did they say?

00:12:13.270 --> 00:12:17.890
They didn't really comment on the scores,

00:12:17.890 --> 00:12:21.810
but they wanted to ask why you have two local colleges in your list.

00:12:21.810 --> 00:12:30.140
They were wondering if you're trying to be considerate about the family financial situation or about me.

00:12:31.140 --> 00:12:32.640
Not at all!

00:12:32.640 --> 00:12:35.390
You're so bad at hiding things.

00:12:37.400 --> 00:12:41.450
Well, I guess that was a factor in my decision.

00:12:42.480 --> 00:12:47.030
I've been living alone since I started high school, and a private one at that.

00:12:48.240 --> 00:12:51.410
And that takes a lot of money,

00:12:51.410 --> 00:12:55.430
whereas you just go to a public high school close to home.

00:12:55.430 --> 00:12:59.380
You always complained that only I seem to get to do what I want.

00:13:00.380 --> 00:13:02.750
I thought you had a point there.

00:13:03.520 --> 00:13:06.130
The local colleges seemed pretty good too.

00:13:08.140 --> 00:13:09.140
Chika?

00:13:09.140 --> 00:13:10.760
You irritate me so much!

00:13:10.760 --> 00:13:11.640
Huh?

00:13:12.220 --> 00:13:13.390
How come?

00:13:13.390 --> 00:13:16.770
That attitude of yours always irritates me.

00:13:16.770 --> 00:13:21.130
You make it sound like I'm living at home and going to a public high school

00:13:21.130 --> 00:13:24.230
even though I don't want to.

00:13:24.230 --> 00:13:29.740
It's just that I'm not ready to live alone and go to a private school yet.

00:13:30.990 --> 00:13:35.000
Just like you're here because you want to be.

00:13:36.120 --> 00:13:42.730
So I find your consideration patronizing.

00:13:43.250 --> 00:13:47.510
By the way, Mom and Dad said they don't have a problem as long as you pay them back when you get a good job.

00:13:47.510 --> 00:13:48.350
Huh?

00:13:51.550 --> 00:13:55.430
Oh, you all already knew Chika-chan was coming?

00:13:55.860 --> 00:13:59.440
We were talking about how it'd be fun to have another gyoza party.

00:13:59.810 --> 00:14:02.190
We're almost done over here,

00:14:02.190 --> 00:14:04.440
but I wonder if Chika's gonna take longer.

00:14:11.180 --> 00:14:13.240
Sorry, Chika.

00:14:13.240 --> 00:14:16.500
As long as you understand.

00:14:17.060 --> 00:14:21.890
You have talent, and you're using it well.

00:14:21.890 --> 00:14:23.270
I think that's amazing.

00:14:24.520 --> 00:14:26.710
I'm cheering for you.

00:14:26.710 --> 00:14:29.970
I want you to aim for the college that you want to go to the most.

00:14:29.970 --> 00:14:31.170
Chika...

00:14:31.590 --> 00:14:33.140
And that's a wrap.

00:14:33.720 --> 00:14:38.680
All that was just what Mom and Dad wanted me to tell you.

00:14:38.680 --> 00:14:39.550
Okay.

00:14:43.040 --> 00:14:44.630
Anyway, th-that's everything.

00:14:44.630 --> 00:14:47.860
I'm done being the messenger!

00:14:49.860 --> 00:14:52.480
Oh, they're ready.

00:14:52.480 --> 00:14:54.270
Okay, I'll be going, then!

00:14:54.270 --> 00:14:56.010
Huh? You're leaving already?

00:14:56.010 --> 00:14:59.610
Nah, I'm throwing a gyoza party with Nori and the others!

00:14:59.610 --> 00:15:00.350
Nori?

00:15:00.350 --> 00:15:03.130
C'mon, I didn't come here just to see you.

00:15:03.480 --> 00:15:07.960
They stuffed the gyoza while I took care of my job!

00:15:08.520 --> 00:15:10.670
Oh, you wanna come too?

00:15:10.670 --> 00:15:12.150
I don't mind.

00:15:13.500 --> 00:15:16.450
And since Hiro-san is the only one with a hotplate,

00:15:16.450 --> 00:15:18.470
it'll be in her room anyway.

00:15:19.860 --> 00:15:21.150
Hiro...

00:15:25.860 --> 00:15:28.440
Sorry we're late.

00:15:28.440 --> 00:15:30.070
Welcome!

00:15:30.070 --> 00:15:33.070
Aw, you all already knew?

00:15:33.070 --> 00:15:35.670
She sent us all a text randomly last night, right?

00:15:35.670 --> 00:15:36.270
Yeah.

00:15:36.270 --> 00:15:38.830
I got a text last night too.

00:15:39.580 --> 00:15:43.090
Why was I the last one to know?

00:15:43.090 --> 00:15:46.710
I figured I'd get everyone to agree first.

00:15:46.710 --> 00:15:50.880
So, what did Chika-chan come all the way here to tell you?

00:15:52.380 --> 00:15:55.510
Something ugly that I'd rather not tell you about.

00:15:55.510 --> 00:15:58.490
Huh? Why? You're no fun.

00:15:59.500 --> 00:16:01.980
Well, I'll tell you after it all gets worked out.

00:16:03.210 --> 00:16:04.230
Just kidding!

00:16:04.980 --> 00:16:08.910
I heard most of it anyway because Chika-chan's voice was loud.

00:16:08.910 --> 00:16:09.690
Yeah!

00:16:12.690 --> 00:16:16.320
This is my first time making gyoza!

00:16:16.320 --> 00:16:18.950
Wow! Thanks, Nazuna!

00:16:18.950 --> 00:16:23.410
Chika, Nazuna made the ones with the weirdest shapes!

00:16:24.980 --> 00:16:26.460
These must be Nazuna's, then!

00:16:26.460 --> 00:16:29.110
No, I made those.

00:16:29.110 --> 00:16:31.330
Huh? What shape are they supposed to be?

00:16:31.330 --> 00:16:32.090
Goldfish?

00:16:32.090 --> 00:16:33.010
Taiyaki!

00:16:33.010 --> 00:16:37.630
You haven't improved since the last gyoza party, have you?

00:16:37.630 --> 00:16:39.100
Really?

00:16:39.100 --> 00:16:41.140
Okay, let's start frying them!

00:16:45.770 --> 00:16:49.400
Add some potato starch to the water around the gyoza like this.

00:16:57.030 --> 00:16:58.280
All right!

00:16:58.620 --> 00:17:01.160
The winged gyoza are done cooking!

00:17:03.660 --> 00:17:05.910
Let's eat!

00:17:18.920 --> 00:17:19.930
It's good!

00:17:19.930 --> 00:17:21.970
It's so hot!

00:17:21.970 --> 00:17:23.190
Juicy!

00:17:23.190 --> 00:17:24.950
The dough is so chewy!

00:17:24.950 --> 00:17:26.870
I've missed this so much!

00:17:26.870 --> 00:17:29.310
Hidamari Apartments' gyoza tastes so freaking good!

00:17:29.310 --> 00:17:31.570
I'm glad you like it! Have some more!

00:17:31.570 --> 00:17:32.690
I will!

00:17:32.940 --> 00:17:36.700
What are you doing for Christmas this year?

00:17:36.700 --> 00:17:41.630
We haven't made any plans yet, but I guess we'll be eating a cake together at least.

00:17:41.630 --> 00:17:42.580
Yeah.

00:17:44.320 --> 00:17:46.830
You're spending your Christmas with just girls again?

00:17:47.580 --> 00:17:53.090
Onee-chan, you haven't managed to snag a single date during your three years of high school?

00:17:53.090 --> 00:17:56.430
Th-There's still time left before I graduate!

00:17:56.430 --> 00:18:00.150
And I have! I just never got around to telling you.

00:18:00.150 --> 00:18:01.430
You did?

00:18:01.430 --> 00:18:04.110
I didn't know either.

00:18:04.110 --> 00:18:05.100
Hiro!

00:18:05.930 --> 00:18:08.370
Besides, I have college entrance exams coming up,

00:18:08.370 --> 00:18:10.930
so I can't afford to play around <i>too</i> much on Christmas!

00:18:11.480 --> 00:18:16.070
Oh yeah, you seniors both have to study.

00:18:17.280 --> 00:18:19.780
Are you trying for art schools?

00:18:19.780 --> 00:18:24.030
Yeah, I'm thinking about going to an art university and then becoming a teacher.

00:18:24.030 --> 00:18:27.010
You mean you want to become an art teacher?

00:18:27.010 --> 00:18:27.660
Yeah!

00:18:27.660 --> 00:18:28.660
Hiro-sensei!

00:18:29.280 --> 00:18:30.650
That has a nice ring to it!

00:18:30.650 --> 00:18:33.370
Aim to be the second Yoshinoya-sensei!

00:18:33.960 --> 00:18:37.930
I don't think I'll be a fun teacher like her,

00:18:38.840 --> 00:18:41.970
but in terms of becoming an art teacher in general, yeah.

00:18:41.970 --> 00:18:46.610
Oh, right. You're not applying for the same schools as Sae, right?

00:18:46.610 --> 00:18:48.350
Huh, really?

00:18:48.350 --> 00:18:52.830
Yeah, I'm applying to colleges with a literature program.

00:18:52.830 --> 00:18:55.230
You're going to study literature?

00:18:56.730 --> 00:19:01.400
I'm sure you'll become a great author!

00:19:01.400 --> 00:19:03.510
That's way off in the future.

00:19:03.510 --> 00:19:05.910
I haven't even been admitted yet.

00:19:05.910 --> 00:19:11.940
But it's hard to imagine Sae-san and
Hiro-san moving on to different schools.

00:19:11.940 --> 00:19:14.250
It's hard to imagine you apart.

00:19:14.840 --> 00:19:19.420
Yeah, and it's even harder to imagine you two graduating.

00:19:19.420 --> 00:19:23.890
You'll be leaving Hidamari
Apartments in just three months.

00:19:25.890 --> 00:19:29.720
Come on, it's too early to think about things like that.

00:19:29.720 --> 00:19:31.430
Yeah, calm down.

00:19:31.430 --> 00:19:37.070
All right! To maintain the status quo at Hidamari Apartments, you two should repeat a year!

00:19:37.070 --> 00:19:38.070
Rejected.

00:19:39.570 --> 00:19:43.800
Although I get sad when I think about graduation,

00:19:43.800 --> 00:19:46.820
we've finally found what we want to do with the rest of our lives.

00:19:46.820 --> 00:19:49.200
So don't worry and cheer for us.

00:19:49.200 --> 00:19:51.710
Sae-san, Hiro-san...

00:19:56.500 --> 00:19:57.500
Then...

00:19:57.840 --> 00:20:01.070
To help Sae-san and Hiro-san get into colleges,

00:20:01.070 --> 00:20:04.490
let's make a Hidamari Cheer Team!

00:20:06.220 --> 00:20:07.470
Cheer team?

00:20:07.470 --> 00:20:09.810
Hidamari Apartment residents will become one

00:20:09.810 --> 00:20:13.710
and do what we can to help Sae-san and Hiro-san get into college!

00:20:13.710 --> 00:20:14.980
Yeah!

00:20:22.780 --> 00:20:25.110
You wanna get into college or not?

00:20:25.110 --> 00:20:26.570
We do!

00:20:26.570 --> 00:20:29.530
Play! Play!

00:20:29.530 --> 00:20:31.450
Sae, Hiro!

00:20:31.450 --> 00:20:34.960
Play, play, Sae, Hiro! Play, play, Sae, Hiro!

00:20:34.960 --> 00:20:37.080
Go for it, go for it, Sae, Hiro!

00:20:37.080 --> 00:20:40.840
Go for it, go for it, Sae, Hiro! Go for it, go for it, Sae, Hiro!

00:20:40.840 --> 00:20:42.340
Yay!

00:20:44.090 --> 00:20:45.720
I appreciate the support.

00:20:45.720 --> 00:20:47.130
Thank you.

00:20:47.130 --> 00:20:49.720
I feel like you've given me new strength.

00:20:49.720 --> 00:20:54.310
Yeah, let us know if there's anything we can do!

00:20:54.310 --> 00:21:00.610
Hidamari Cheer Team will be active every day until you get your acceptance letters!

00:21:00.610 --> 00:21:02.320
What? Every day?

00:21:02.320 --> 00:21:04.570
Play! Play!

00:21:06.570 --> 00:21:07.610
Hey!

00:21:10.950 --> 00:21:13.530
That was a great bath!

00:21:14.870 --> 00:21:17.500
Are you ready to go home tomorrow?

00:21:17.500 --> 00:21:19.250
Yeah, I am.

00:21:19.250 --> 00:21:22.930
All right, then let's get to bed before you get too chilly.

00:21:22.930 --> 00:21:23.880
Okay!

00:21:27.760 --> 00:21:28.790
I'm turning off the light.

00:21:28.790 --> 00:21:29.760
Go ahead.

00:21:33.240 --> 00:21:36.880
Chika, thanks for today.

00:21:36.880 --> 00:21:39.330
Huh? What did I do?

00:21:39.930 --> 00:21:41.270
Just saying.

00:21:41.270 --> 00:21:43.230
You're not too cold, right?

00:21:43.230 --> 00:21:43.900
I'm fine.

00:21:44.280 --> 00:21:46.830
Feel free to join legs with me.

00:21:48.700 --> 00:21:49.410
Yeah.

00:21:50.500 --> 00:21:53.910
I think coming to Hidamari Apartments worked out well for you.

00:21:56.600 --> 00:21:57.620
Yeah.

00:21:57.620 --> 00:21:59.120
Night.

00:21:59.120 --> 00:22:00.120
Good night.

00:22:10.860 --> 00:22:13.140
Let's get in the Christmas spirit!

00:22:13.140 --> 00:22:16.980
Run-run-ru, Run-run-ru, Christmas!

00:22:16.980 --> 00:22:18.400
Something sounded off.

00:22:18.400 --> 00:22:20.080
Should we try it again?

00:22:20.080 --> 00:22:23.820
Run-run-ru, Run-run-ru, Christmas!

00:22:23.820 --> 00:22:24.980
Oh, that was perfect!

00:22:24.980 --> 00:22:27.660
Sorry, I didn't sing this time.

00:22:27.660 --> 00:22:32.060
Next time: "December 22nd, So You Were the Big Sister."

00:22:32.060 --> 00:22:35.880
"December 21st-24th, A Song I Faintly Remember."

00:22:35.880 --> 00:22:39.140
We'll be waiting at Hidamari Apartments, so come visit us!
